WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.989
Let's go next to our caller from the nine
five, four area code.

00:00:03.989 --> 00:00:05.919
Who's calling today from nine five four

00:00:05.919 --> 00:00:13.730
Joelle, Joelle, what's up before lardo?

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:20.010
Um, yeah, I'm a Andrew yanked supporter and
um, uh, I was just, I just wanted to get your

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:25.560
thoughts on the coming automation wave and
I know you don't, you're not a big fan of

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:31.289
is UBI or universal basic income, but uh,
Bernie wants, his answer for automation would

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:33.050
be a federal jobs guarantee.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:38.460
I was wondering, what would you, uh, what
would those two options for automation, what

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.510
would you prefer if like in the future you
had to pick one?

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:47.920
So I'm not against UBI, I just don't see UBI
as the solution to automation.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:53.079
I've been critical before when Andrew Yang
said that UBI, any dollar you get from UBI,

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:54.219
you lose from other benefits.

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:55.670
I want UBI to be additive.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:58.979
The idea is to raise people's standard of
living, not to just change where they're getting

00:00:58.979 --> 00:00:59.979
money from.

00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:00.979
So, so I'm not against UBI.

00:01:00.979 --> 00:01:05.720
In fact, I've been talking about UBI, including
with Andrew Yang on this program much longer

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.729
than almost any other show has.

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:11.049
I just don't see UBI as the deal as the way
to deal with automation.

00:01:11.049 --> 00:01:15.280
I think that, um, there has to be some kind
of bridge solution.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:17.740
There are going to be jobs automated away.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.100
It's just the reality.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.659
And what we have to think about is which industries
are likely to be hardest hit?

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:27.840
What kind of retraining can we do if people
who are going to lose jobs for moving towards

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:35.009
industries that are going to flourish or potentially
even grow as we continue to move forward.

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:41.189
And for me, it's, it's not about jobs guarantee
versus using UBI to pay people who lose jobs

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:42.189
to automation.

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:43.920
These are kind of all disjointed things.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:50.010
I think we need sort of a much more holistic
approach and UBI for me is very interesting,

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.499
but not the way to deal with automation.

00:01:52.499 --> 00:01:55.170
All right, thanks.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.631
Thank you very much man.

00:01:56.631 --> 00:01:57.631
I appreciate it.

00:01:57.631 --> 00:01:58.631
All right, very good.

00:01:58.631 --> 00:01:59.631
Thank you so much for the call.

00:01:59.631 --> 00:02:02.479
We will go to a break and come back with more
right after this.

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:04.929
Sorry to everybody I was not able to pick
up on.

00:02:04.929 --> 00:02:06.009
We always get more calls

00:02:06.009 --> 00:02:08.400
then the number we can take, but that's a
good sign.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.400
That's a good problem to have.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.590
Quick break back after this,

